# Repo-root Docker build context (used by pipeline/Dockerfile, which builds the Rust pipeline
# binaries). The context is the repo ROOT — not pipeline/ — because `pipeline-core`/`replay`
# `include_str!` a handful of refdata files from the repo root at build time (src/data/*.json,
# scripts/data-pipeline/replay-rs/data/maps.tsv). This ignore file keeps the context lean: send
# only the Rust workspace + those refdata files, never the multi-GB build caches / site assets.

# Secrets — must NEVER reach the Docker daemon or be baked into a layer.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Build caches & large generated trees.
**/target
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/node_modules
**/*.egg-info
data-cache
dist
.astro
.pagefind
coverage
test-results
playwright-report
*.log

# VCS/metadata not needed for the build.
.git
.github

# Site / analyzer assets the pipeline image doesn't need.
analyzer
public

# scripts/ is multi-GB (crawl outputs, DuckDB) — keep ONLY the one maps.tsv the Rust build embeds.
scripts/**
!scripts/data-pipeline
!scripts/data-pipeline/replay-rs
!scripts/data-pipeline/replay-rs/data
!scripts/data-pipeline/replay-rs/data/**
